{"id": "d53c0424b3cba095:tutorial:gpt-6-luna:", "source_id": "d53c0424b3cba095", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/save-and-invest/learn-about-investment-options", "topic": "Learn About Investment Options", "subtopic": null, "content_type": "tutorial", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Stocks, bonds, mutual funds and ETFs are the most common asset categories.", "question": null, "answer": "Investment options come in different asset categories. Stocks, bonds, mutual funds, and exchange-traded funds (ETFs) are among the most common. Before choosing an investment, understand its risks and the fees involved in buying, selling, and holding it.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 178}}
{"id": "d53c0424b3cba095:qa:gpt-6-luna:", "source_id": "d53c0424b3cba095", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/save-and-invest/learn-about-investment-options", "topic": "Learn About Investment Options", "subtopic": null, "content_type": "qa", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "directly_supported", "source_evidence": "Before you make any investment, understand the risks of the investment and make sure the risks are appropriate for you. You’ll also want to understand the fees associated with the buying, selling, and holding the investment.", "question": "What should you understand before making an investment?", "answer": "Understand the investment’s risks and whether they are appropriate for you. Also learn about fees for buying, selling, and holding it.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 166}}
{"id": "d53c0424b3cba095:misconception:gpt-6-luna:", "source_id": "d53c0424b3cba095", "source_url": "https://www.investor.gov/introduction-investing/investing-basics/save-and-invest/learn-about-investment-options", "topic": "Learn About Investment Options", "subtopic": null, "content_type": "misconception", "teacher_model": "gpt-6-luna", "generation_status": "generated", "skip_reason": null, "grounding": "derived_from_source", "source_evidence": "Other asset categories include real estate, precious metals and other commodities, and private equity.", "question": "Misconception: Stocks, bonds, mutual funds, and ETFs are the only asset categories investors can choose from.", "answer": "These are common asset categories, but they are not the only ones. Other categories include real estate, precious metals and other commodities, and private equity. Investments in these categories typically have category-specific risks.", "formula_latex": null, "source_evidence_exact_match": true, "review_status": "unverified", "api_usage": {"input_tokens": 900, "output_tokens": 198}}
